abstract: >-
  MATLAB code that solves the sine-Gordon equation on a network, a graph whose edges carry the equation and whose
  vertices join them through the continuity of the solution and Kirchhoff's condition. Each edge carries a uniform
  lattice on which the equation is advanced by the explicit leapfrog scheme, and the value at each vertex is the mean of
  the values at the nearest nodes of the edges that meet there. The shipped script computes three kinks of speed 0.95
  that cross the vertices of a graph with four vertices and six edges, collide and come back.
